  "method": "Each triplet runs native, Durante, native on the same ELF with empty stdin and the frozen expected eight output bytes. Four rounds rotate pair order and reverse within-pair order twice. Use final wait4 child user + system nanoseconds. Score every prediction against its eight-native median. A case passes only if all four predictions are within 20%. Report the minimum native time and (max-min)/median against the quality thresholds separately.",
  "analysis": "For the eight named contrasts report median numerator/denominator native and frozen prediction ratios, observed native ratio range and four paired round ratios; compare instruction, modeled cycles and byte ratios. Report observed vs disassembly-derived instruction/byte totals. Additionally compute the best possible nonnegative two-term worst error over all case medians and over optimistically unpaired observed ranges, including the range bound for each contrast. Only the coefficients frozen from the preceding Rust study are predictive. This is a mechanistic benchmark and does not set verdict times.",
  "purpose": "Prospective follow-up on a fresh VM after inspecting the initial dependency results. Separate memory access order from table initialization, and measure how changing the instruction that zeros the high dividend changes predictions versus native times.",
  "primary_protocol_sha256": "fd9c645d37b77bedce6655bdf6d013a8748859d7992a7b938013247f99369464",
  "primary_dataset_sha256": "1683bc9c5b549a6d87772e10ad84c6372a2043aeeace65bca565e57416dc7fbf",
  "hypotheses": [
    "With identical initialization, address set, hot code and byte counts, a scrambled successor order can cost more native CPU than an adjacent order. The full elapsed process includes identical setup. Each treatment visits each table entry exactly 33 times through its selected field; both four-byte fields are in the same cache line and page for each record.",
    "The original local diagnostic observed the old-high-register dependency in the XOR spelling. Replacing xor edx,edx with mov edx,0 changes the static latency ratio without changing the high dividend or div/rem stream. Compare both native dataflows and the change in model ratio on GCE. This claim is prospective for native CPU timing only."
  ],
